    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.97) and **Seiya Suzuki** (65.95), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms in Colin Rea and Jeffrey Springs. **Austin Riley** remains a priority start at 63.69; while the matchup against Corbin looks standard on paper, his Elite BvP data and the situational advantage of facing a lefty propel his score significantly above his base projection. We are also leaning heavily on the high-floor speed of **Corbin Carroll** (61.03) and **James Wood** (60.51). **James Wood** is particularly intriguing, as his elite xwOBA metrics and favorable leadoff spot allow him to transcend a neutral platoon, keeping our stolen base potential high despite the presence of competent opposing starters.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros** (49.76), who fell just shy of the active roster threshold. While his SP Skill rating against Ure\u00f1a was quite strong, the negative drag from his assumed #8 spot in the order and the presence of elite defensive catchers behind the dish ultimately made him the odd man out in favor of the higher-upside profiles like **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**. We continue to monitor the status of **Mickey Moniak**, who remains on the IL, alongside depth pieces like **Jose Caballero**, **Cole Young**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Carson Williams**. \n\nCaution is advised regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Brice Turang**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Seiya Suzuki**. While we have modeled these based on historical positioning, any shuffle in the batting order\u2014specifically dropping these players toward the bottom of the lineup\u2014could trigger a sharp decline in their daily efficiency score. Furthermore, we face a stiff challenge in the **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** slots against Shohei Ohtani; despite their strong individual profiles, the elite talent on the mound necessitates a close watch on their early-game plate appearances.",
